0..77 Comment "//! A rule written as an equation, `<=>`: one term spelled two ways, with the"
78..157 Comment "//! left side the one a reader would rewrite to. The order of terms chooses the"
158..219 Comment "//! direction, so `x <=> S(P(x))` still runs `S(P(x))` to `x`"
220..295 Comment "//! [Huet-1980-confluent_reductions]. The integers are named apart from the"
296..352 Comment "//! base\'s, whose rules are written the other way round."
353..356 Comment "//!"
357..402 Comment "//! - cites: [Huet-1980-confluent_reductions]"
403..406 Comment "//!"
407..511 Comment "//! [Huet-1980-confluent_reductions]: https://doi.org/10.1145/322217.322230 \"Huet, Confluent reductions\""
513..579 Comment "/// The integers with their first rule written smaller side first."
